    "question": {
      "text": "If $A$, $B$ and $C$ are mutually exclusive such that $5P(B)=8P(A)$, $4P(C)=3P(B)$ and $19P(A\\cup B)=13$ then $P(A\\cup B\\cup C)$ is ________.",
      "type": "MCQ",
      "options": [
        {
          "label": "A",
          "text": "$0.75$"
        },
        {
          "label": "B",
          "text": "$1$"
        },
        {
          "label": "C",
          "text": "$0.625$"
        },
        {
          "label": "D",
          "text": "Cannot be determined"
        }
      ],
      "marks": null,
      "negativeMarks": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
    "answer": {
      "correctOption": "B",
      "correctText": "$1$",
      "explanation": "Given $5P(B)=8P(A)$ and $4P(C)=3P(B)$\n$$P(A)=\\frac{5}{8}P(B)\\quad\\text{and}\\quad P(C)=\\frac{3}{4}P(B).$$\nNow $19P(A\\cup B)=13\\Rightarrow P(A\\cup B)=\\frac{13}{19}$.\nSince $A$ and $B$ are mutually exclusive,\n$$P(A)+P(B)=\\frac{13}{19}.$$\nTherefore,\n$$\\frac{5}{8}P(B)+P(B)=\\frac{13}{19},$$\nso $P(B)=\\frac{8}{19}$.\nNow\n$$P(A\\cup B\\cup C)=P(A)+P(B)+P(C)=\\frac58P(B)+P(B)+\\frac34P(B)=\\frac{19}{8}P(B)=1.$$\nChoice (B)",
      "status": "confirmed"
    },
    "classification": {
      "subject": "Probability and Statistics",
      "topic": null,
      "subtopic": null,
      "tags": []
    },
