      "marks": null,
      "negativeMarks": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
    "answer": {
      "correctOption": "A",
      "correctText": "$0.125$",
      "explanation": "The total number of passengers = 240.\nLet $S$, $B$ and $P$ denote the sets of passengers who like sandwich, burger and pizza respectively.\n$$n(S)=140,\\ n(B)=110,\\ n(P)=90,$$\n$$n(S\\cap B)=40,\\ n(B\\cap P)=40,\\ n(P\\cap S)=50$$\nand $n(S\\cap B\\cap P)=30$.\nProbability that a randomly selected passenger likes only pizza\n$$=\\frac{n(P)-n(P\\cap S)-n(B\\cap P)+n(S\\cap B\\cap P)}{240}$$\n$$=\\frac{90-50-40+30}{240}=\\frac18=0.125.$$\nChoice (A)",
