      "text": "An unbiased coin is tossed until it shows up the same face in two consecutive throws. What is the probability that the number of tosses is not more than 4?",
      "type": "MCQ",
      "options": [
        {
          "label": "A",
          "text": "$\\frac34$"
        },
        {
          "label": "B",
          "text": "$\\frac18$"
        },
        {
          "label": "C",
          "text": "$\\frac78$"
        },
        {
          "label": "D",
          "text": "$\\frac14$"
        }
      ],
      "marks": null,
      "negativeMarks": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
    "answer": {
      "correctOption": "C",
      "correctText": "$\\frac78$",
      "explanation": "The number of tosses may be 2 or 3 or 4.\nThe possible cases and their corresponding probabilities:\nCase 1: $HH$ OR $TT\\rightarrow2\\left(\\frac12\\right)^2$.\nCase 2: $HTT$ OR $THH\\rightarrow2\\left(\\frac12\\right)^3$.\nCase 3: $HTHH$ OR $THTT\\rightarrow2\\left(\\frac12\\right)^4$.\nHence, the required probability is\n$$2\\left[\\frac14+\\frac18+\\frac1{16}\\right]=\\frac78.$$\nChoice (C)",
      "status": "confirmed"
    },
