    "answer": {
      "correctOption": "B",
      "correctText": "$1:69$",
      "explanation": "We have 4 five rupee coins, 3 two rupee coins and 3 one rupee coins.\nFor the draw to yield a maximum amount, of the 6 coins drawn 4 should be five rupee coins and 2 should be two rupee coins. The required probability is\n$$\\frac{{}^4C_4\\times{}^3C_2}{{}^{10}C_6}=\\frac3{210}=\\frac1{70}.$$\nHence, odds in favour are favourable ways : unfavourable ways $=1:69$.\nChoice (B)",
