    "question": {
      "text": "An urn A contains 6 white balls and 7 black balls. And urn B contains 8 white balls and 6 black balls. A person draws a ball at random from one of the two urns. It turns out to be black. What is the probability that the ball was drawn from urn A?",
      "type": "MCQ",
      "options": [
        {
          "label": "A",
          "text": "$\\frac7{14}$"
        },
        {
          "label": "B",
          "text": "$\\frac{49}{88}$"
        },
        {
          "label": "C",
          "text": "$\\frac{39}{88}$"
        },
        {
          "label": "D",
          "text": "None of the above"
        }
      ],
      "marks": null,
      "negativeMarks": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
    "answer": {
      "correctOption": "B",
      "correctText": "$\\frac{49}{88}$",
      "explanation": "Probability of selecting urn A is $P(A)=\\frac12$ and that of selecting urn B is $P(B)=\\frac12$.\nProbability of drawing a black ball (event $E$) when urn A is selected\n$$P\\left(\\frac{E}{A}\\right)=\\frac{{}^7C_1}{{}^{13}C_1}$$\nand probability of $E$ when urn B is selected\n$$P\\left(\\frac{E}{B}\\right)=\\frac{{}^6C_1}{{}^{14}C_1}.$$\nTherefore,\n$$P(E)=P(A)P\\left(\\frac EA\\right)+P(B)P\\left(\\frac EB\\right).$$\nThe required probability\n$$P\\left(\\frac AE\\right)=\\frac{P(A)P(E/A)}{P(E)}=\\frac{49}{88}.$$\nChoice (B)",
      "status": "confirmed"
    },
