      "text": "In a book of 500 pages, there are 50 typing errors. Assuming that the number of errors per page follows poisson distribution, find the probability that randomly chosen 5 pages will contain no error.",
      "type": "MCQ",
      "options": [
        {
          "label": "A",
          "text": "$0.6065$"
        },
        {
          "label": "B",
          "text": "$0.6078$"
        },
        {
          "label": "C",
          "text": "$0.6538$"
        },
        {
          "label": "D",
          "text": "$0.3935$"
        }
      ],
      "marks": null,
      "negativeMarks": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
    "answer": {
      "correctOption": "A",
      "correctText": "$0.6065$",
      "explanation": "Average number of errors per page $\\lambda=\\frac{50}{500}=\\frac1{10}$.\nAverage number of errors per 5 pages $=5\\times\\frac1{10}=\\frac12$.\nProbability of $k$ errors per page is\n$$P(x=k)=\\frac{\\lambda^k}{k!}e^{-\\lambda}.$$\nHere $k=0$, so\n$$P(k=0)=e^{-1/2}.$$\nProbability that a random sample of 5 pages has no error $=e^{-0.5}=0.6065$.\nChoice (A)",
      "status": "confirmed"
    },
    "classification": {
