    "question": {
      "text": "The continuous random variable $X$ is uniformly distributed with mean 2 and variance 12. Find $P(X>0)$.",
      "type": "MCQ",
      "options": [
        {
          "label": "A",
          "text": "$\\frac13$"
        },
        {
          "label": "B",
          "text": "$\\frac45$"
        },
        {
          "label": "C",
          "text": "$\\frac23$"
        },
        {
          "label": "D",
          "text": "$\\frac15$"
        }
      ],
      "marks": null,
      "negativeMarks": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
    "answer": {
      "correctOption": "C",
      "correctText": "$\\frac23$",
      "explanation": "We know that $X$ is uniform random variable in the interval $[a,b]$ then\n$$p(x)=\\frac1{b-a},\\quad a<x<b$$\nand\n$$\\text{mean}=\\frac{a+b}{2},\\qquad \\text{variance}=\\frac{(b-a)^2}{12}.$$\nGiven mean $=2$,\n$$\\frac{a+b}{2}=2\\Rightarrow a+b=4.\\tag{1}$$\nVariance $=12$,\n$$\\frac{(b-a)^2}{12}=12\\Rightarrow(b-a)^2=144\\Rightarrow b-a=12.\\tag{2}$$\nSolving (1) and (2), $a=-4,b=8$.\nTherefore\n$$P(X>0)=\\int_0^8\\frac1{12}\\,dx=\\frac8{12}=\\frac23.$$\nChoice (C)",
      "status": "confirmed"
    },
