    "question": {
      "text": "Bag $A$ contains 9 white balls and 5 green balls. Bag $B$ contains 6 white balls and 7 green balls. One ball is drawn from bag $A$ and is placed in bag $B$. Now one ball is drawn at random from bag $B$. It is found that the ball is green. Find the probability that white ball is transferred from bag $A$.",
      "type": "MCQ",
      "options": [
        {
          "label": "A",
          "text": "$\\frac{20}{103}$"
        },
        {
          "label": "B",
          "text": "$\\frac{63}{103}$"
        },
        {
          "label": "C",
          "text": "$\\frac{80}{103}$"
        },
        {
          "label": "D",
          "text": "$\\frac{75}{103}$"
        }
      ],
      "marks": null,
      "negativeMarks": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
    "answer": {
      "correctOption": "B",
      "correctText": "$\\frac{63}{103}$",
      "explanation": "Let $B_1$: transfer of white ball to bag $B$.\n$B_2$: transfer of green ball to bag $B$.\n$$P(B_1)=\\frac9{14};\\qquad P(B_2)=\\frac5{14}.$$\nLet $E$ be the event of drawing a green ball from bag $B$ after transfer.\n$$P\\left(\\frac E{B_1}\\right)=\\frac7{14}$$\nand\n$$P\\left(\\frac E{B_2}\\right)=\\frac8{14}.$$\nTherefore\n$$P(E)=P(B_1)P(E/B_1)+P(B_2)P(E/B_2)$$\n$$=\\frac9{14}\\cdot\\frac7{14}+\\frac5{14}\\cdot\\frac8{14}=\\frac{103}{196}.$$\nThe required probability\n$$P\\left(\\frac{B_1}{E}\\right)=\\frac{P(B_1)P(E/B_1)}{P(E)}\n=\\frac{63}{103}.$$\nChoice (B)",
      "status": "confirmed"
    },
