    "answer": {
      "correctOption": "C",
      "correctText": "$\\frac13$",
      "explanation": "Let $A$ be the event that the number 3 appears atleast once.\n$B$ be the event that sum of the numbers appearing is 7.\n$A\\cap B$ be the event that the sum is 7 and 3 appear atleast once.\n$$P(B)=\\frac6{36}\\Rightarrow P(A\\cap B)=\\frac2{36}.$$\n$A/B$ denotes atleast one number show 3 while the sum of the numbers is 7.\n$$P\\left(\\frac AB\\right)=\\frac{P(B\\cap A)}{P(B)}\n=\\frac{2/36}{6/36}=\\frac13.$$\nChoice (C)",
      "status": "confirmed"
