      "explanation": "We know that variance $(x,x+3,x+5,x+7,x+10)$\n$=$ variance $(0,3,5,7,10)$.\n$$AM(0,3,5,7,10)=\\frac{0+3+5+7+10}{5}=\\frac{25}{5}=5.$$\n$$\\text{Variance}(0,3,5,7,10)=\\frac{\\sum(x_i-A)^2}{n}$$\n$$=\\frac{(0-5)^2+(3-5)^2+(5-5)^2+(7-5)^2+(10-5)^2}{5}$$\n$$=\\frac{25+4+0+4+25}{5}=\\frac{58}{5}=11.6.$$\nChoice (B)",
